# SoftDevice Controller (SDC) BLE controller integration.
#
# This is a personal experiment vendoring sdk-nrf's BLE controller integration
# into our config so the standard ZMK build can use Nordic's SoftDevice
# Controller from nrfxlib instead of Zephyr's built-in BLE controller.
#
# Sources are vendored from https://github.com/nrfconnect/sdk-nrf @ main:
#
#   subsys/bluetooth/controller/   -> controller/
#   lib/multithreading_lock/       -> lib/multithreading_lock/
#   dts/bindings/bluetooth/        -> dts/bindings/bluetooth/
#
# These files are © Nordic Semiconductor ASA and licensed under
# LicenseRef-Nordic-5-Clause; see the SPDX headers in each file.
#
# This integration also requires `nrfxlib` to be present as a Zephyr module
# (added via config/west.yml), which provides:
#   - The SoftDevice Controller binary library (libsoftdevice_controller_*.a)
#   - The Multi-Protocol Service Layer (MPSL)
#   - Headers for sdc.h, sdc_hci.h, sdc_soc.h, mpsl.h, etc.
#
# Status: experimental. Untested on hardware; may need additional Kconfig glue
# discovered through CI iterations.
